// Network sync test scene, spawned by the SERVER only (main.cpp): its Network components register
// there, get server-minted netIds, and the whole scene materializes on every client via Spawn
// replication - clients spawn nothing shared themselves, their scenes can differ arbitrarily.
// Gizmo-drag a render-only cube on the SERVER and the client copy follows at the snapshot rate;
// drag one on the CLIENT and it returns to the server's state on the next keyframe (nothing sends
// client -> server). The dynamic physics cubes drop onto the static ground and tumble: both sides
// simulate, the client corrects its bodies toward the server's poses/velocities and sleeps them
// when the server's sleep. Press K on either instance to fire the "NetPing" network event (logged
// on every connected instance).
Prefab networkTest
	Name "Network Test"
	Position 0 0 0
	Rotation 0 -0 0
	Scale 1
	Component Scene
		Entity NetGround
			Position 1 -1 3
			Scale 50
			Component Render
				ObjectContainer baseshapes
				Node Plane
				Type StaticMesh
			Component Physics
				Body Static
				Shape Box
				HalfExtents 1.0 0.01 1.0
				Offset 0 0 0
		Entity NetPhysCube1
			Position 0.6 3 3.2
			Scale 0.25
			Component Render
				ObjectContainer wireshapes
				Node Cube
				Type StaticMesh
			Component Physics
				Body Dynamic
				Shape Box
				HalfExtents 1 1 1
				Restitution 0.3
				Density 400
				ContactEvents true
			Component Network
		Entity NetPhysCube2
			Position 1.4 4.2 2.8
			Scale 0.25
			Component Render
				ObjectContainer wireshapes
				Node Cube
				Type StaticMesh
			Component Physics
				Body Dynamic
				Shape Box
				HalfExtents 1 1 1
				Restitution 0.3
				Density 400
				ContactEvents true
			Component Network
